  "body": "## Result\n\nFor the generic immutable-source, one-dirty-connector F2 interface with five sources and all31 nonzero output masks, this proves the exact complete-map cost for every36 independently positive source/readout prices:\n\n`OPT = 2 sum(b_j) + 2 sum(a_m) + 2 min({b_0,...,b_4} union {a_m : popcount(m)=3 or5})`.\n\nExactly16 componentwise minimal call profiles exist over **all finite legal words**. Each starts with two calls per map and adds two calls to one of five sources or eleven heavy-odd-mask readouts. All16 profiles have literal74-call dirty-state witnesses and each is uniquely exposed by positive rational prices. A cheap even-mask readout cannot absorb the surcharge: all prices10 except a_3=1 gives722, not704; changing the cheap mask to31 attains704.\n\n## Why the word-length domain is complete\n\nEvery active map count is even and at least two. Any word with at least12 source events has a source count at least four and is componentwise dominated by an explicit repeated-source witness. Exactly10 source events reduce to945 canonical pairings; each misses a weight3-or5 mask and therefore needs at least four readouts of that output. Both singleton-missing weight orbits are attained. Thus no longer schedule can beat the16-vector frontier. Two code-disjoint engines compare all29295 readout costs, including42 six-readout cases rather than capping them at four.\n\n## Credit, scope and novelty\n\nPackage: `research/connector-all-tariff-optimum/`, eight added files. Base e112d71c8d7bb32435debcc54df932593dd8223a; full commit4caa7660fa4a31c4cfeaf177fabc3b56549dd065.\n\nCredit Ross Richardson PR943/934 for the generic contract, paired-prefix criterion and universal source words; Cinna Davis PR1770 for the one-vector182 optimum and PR1811 for the odd-parity-family obstruction. The new result is the entire36-variable tariff theorem and irredundant frontier, not those inherited mechanisms or another unit-query census. Exact heads, SHA256/Git-blob pins and attribution are in SOURCES.json.\n\nIndependent chooser seed9c083f6b391fc18192cb0990085ca4ed; recursive-interfaces; connector-alphabet-change. Scope explicitly **changed**: no operation alphabet is extended, so this is a caller-tariff oracle side result, not success at the original mechanism gate. No supplier occurrence, complete physical tariff, recursive moment gain, new kappa, selected frontier edit or formal-kernel claim. Word-dependent admission, preparation, dispatch and routing remain separately charged. Final live overlap found PR2056 pair-source calls and PR2050 output-bank-mixing erasure, distinct contracts/results documented in README.\n\n## Exercised verification\n\nCPython3.12.12, Darwin arm64:\n\n- `uv run --python 3.12 --no-project python -I -O -B research/connector-all-tariff-optimum/verify.py --write-result research/connector-all-tariff-optimum/RESULT.json` passed the focused final generation/smoke.\n- `uv run --python 3.12 --no-project python scripts/research_package.py --package research/connector-all-tariff-optimum` passed:945pairings,16profiles,3552dirty-basis forward/inverse case pairs,9semantic controls,4behavioral tests including live-source/receipt corruption, no-overwrite receipts and optimized read-only noGit relocation.\n- Parent separately reviewed the unrestricted-word proof and independently replayed the registered package before publication authorization.\n\nNo full repository suite, selected cold replay or hosted CI success is claimed.\n\nClaim: #research-claim-and-completion-record\n\nPrepared for adamgall with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in proof, code, experiments and writing. Apache-2.0; no independent human review claimed.\n\n## Research claim and completion record\n\nStatus: completed. The claim record is preserved here so this PR is self-contained. Historical coordination links in the committed research metadata refer to this record; the separate coordination discussion is being removed.\n\nDONE \u2014 claim released. PR2063: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2063 ; full head4caa7660fa4a31c4cfeaf177fabc3b56549dd065, base e112d71c8d7bb32435debcc54df932593dd8223a. Package research/connector-all-tariff-optimum/. Seed9c083f6b391fc18192cb0990085ca4ed; recursive-interfaces, connector-alphabet-change with scope explicitly changed to full tariff optimality, not a new operation.\n\nEstablished for the generic five-source/all31-mask immutable-source dirty connector and all36 independent positive complete-map prices: OPT=2sum(b,a)+2min({five B prices} union {A_m:weight(m)=3or5}). Exactly16 componentwise minimal profiles over ALL finite words; each has a74-call arbitrary-dirty witness. Any >=12-source-event word is dominated by a repeated-source witness; every10-event path misses a heavy odd mask. All945canonical pairings and29295exact readout costs are checked by independent algorithms, including42 six-readout costs.\n\nObserved CPython3.12.12 focused and registered replay PASS:945pairings/16profiles/3552dirty forward-inverse basis pairs/9semantic controls plus4behavioral tests. Parent separately reviewed and replayed before publication. Reproduce: uv run --python 3.12 --no-project python scripts/research_package.py --package research/connector-all-tariff-optimum . No hostedCI or selected cold replay claimed.\n\nCredit Ross Richardson PR943/934, Cinna Davis PR1770 one-vector182 optimum and PR1811 odd-family obstruction; exact heads and pins retained. PR2056 pair-source operations and PR2050 output-bank-mixing erasure were read before submission and are distinct. No selected caller, physical runtime optimum or kappa gain. Substantial OpenAI Codex assistance, Apache-2.0, no independent human review.\n",
